From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: suckbluefrog <suckbluefrog@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 10 Jul 2026 00:00:00 +000
Subject: [PATCH] Build C sources as GNU17 with GCC 15

quasi88 uses legacy C callback declarations such as:

  typedef void (*Q8tkSignalFunc)();

Under GCC 15's newer default C dialect this is treated as a no-argument
prototype, which turns the existing q8tk callbacks into incompatible
function pointer errors. Build the C side as GNU17 so the existing
old-style callback ABI keeps its historical semantics.

Signed-off-by: suckbluefrog <suckbluefrog@proton.me>
---
 Makefile | 1 +
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+)

diff --git a/Makefile b/Makefile
index 3d2a501..9d93a7c 100644
--- a/Makefile
+++ b/Makefile
@@ -596,6 +596,7 @@ FLAGS += $(ENDIANNESS_DEFINES) $(WARNINGS) -DSTDC_HEADERS -D__STDC_LIMIT_MACROS
 
 CXXFLAGS += $(FLAGS)
 CFLAGS += $(FLAGS)
+CFLAGS += -std=gnu17 -Wno-error=incompatible-pointer-types
 
 OBJOUT   = -o 
 LINKOUT  = -o 
